# {{hospitalName}} Patient Records System

## Overview
This document describes the patient records system for {{hospitalName}}. The system will manage electronic health records (EHR) with strict compliance to healthcare regulations including HIPAA, GDPR, and local data protection laws.

## Regulatory Compliance Requirements

### HIPAA Compliance
- Protected Health Information (PHI) encryption at rest and in transit
- Access controls and audit logging
- Business Associate Agreements (BAAs)
- Regular security risk assessments
- Employee training on HIPAA requirements

### GDPR Compliance
- Data minimization principles
- Right to access, rectify, and erase personal data
- Data portability
- Privacy by design implementation
- Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs)

### Local Regulations
- Compliance with {{country}} healthcare data protection laws
- Mandatory reporting of data breaches
- Patient consent management
- Retention policies for medical records

## Functional Requirements

### Patient Management
- **Patient Registration**: Capture demographic and contact information
- **Patient Search**: Search by name, ID, date of birth, or medical record number
- **Patient Updates**: Update patient information with audit trail
- **Patient Merge/Duplicate Management**: Identify and resolve duplicate records
- **Patient Deceased Management**: Mark patients as deceased with appropriate notifications

### Medical Records
- **Electronic Health Records (EHR)**: Comprehensive patient medical history
- **Vital Signs Tracking**: Blood pressure, heart rate, temperature, weight, height
- **Medication Management**: Prescription tracking, drug interactions, allergies
- **Lab Results Management**: Integration with lab systems, result tracking
- **Imaging Integration**: DICOM image viewing and management
- **Clinical Notes**: SOAP notes, progress notes, discharge summaries
- **Care Plans**: Treatment plans, goals, interventions
- **Referrals**: Referral tracking and management

### Appointment Scheduling
- **Appointment Booking**: Schedule appointments with providers
- **Waitlist Management**: Manage patient waitlists
- **Appointment Reminders**: Automated SMS/email reminders
- **Resource Scheduling**: Room, equipment, and staff scheduling
- **Appointment Modifications**: Reschedule, cancel, or modify appointments

### Billing and Insurance
- **Insurance Verification**: Real-time insurance eligibility verification
- **Charge Capture**: Automated charge capture from clinical documentation
- **Claims Management**: Electronic claims submission and tracking
- **Payment Processing**: Patient payment collection and management
- **Reporting**: Financial and operational reporting

### Reporting and Analytics
- **Clinical Quality Reports**: Quality metrics and clinical outcomes
- **Operational Reports**: Appointment utilization, provider productivity
- **Financial Reports**: Revenue, collections, accounts receivable
- **Population Health**: Patient population analysis and reporting
- **Regulatory Reports**: Compliance reporting for government agencies

